## Autonomy surface (the ask-set)

<!-- Native allow/ask/deny — do NOT enumerate an allowlist. `deny`/`ask` hold even
     under bypassPermissions, so start from "everything safe runs" and resolve the
     borders only. (autonomy-conventions.md.) -->

- **Deny (never run):** base destructive config + anything conflicting with a
  registered ADR or existing code. This-workflow additions: ____
- **Pre-authorized (run without asking):** normally-prompting ops this workflow may
  run unattended: ____
- **Always-ask (pause every time):** outward publication only. Defaults:
  `git push`/publish/deploy/release. NOT `git commit`, deps, or additive migrations.
  Add/remove for this workflow: ____
- **Autonomous + log:** everything else safe, additive, non-breaking — including a
  class-(b) emergent sub-unit appended to the work-list. Proceed; verify the
  assumption (investigate, don't guess) and log it. A class-(c) emergent decision the
  work itself reveals is the one legitimate mid-run interrupt — rare; preserve it.

